  <div class="post-content"><p>Tax season has already started, and thousands of Latino families are asking the same questions: When do I need to file? How much will I get back? What documents do I need? Am I better off doing my taxes on my own or with a professional?</p><p>At <strong>Guzman Tax & Accounting</strong>, we help Latino individuals and businesses file correctly, avoid costly mistakes, and maximize their legal benefits.</p><h2>When Is the Filing Deadline for 2026?</h2><p>The traditional deadline to file your return is <strong>April 15, 2026</strong> (unless the IRS announces changes). If you need more time, you can request an extension until October 15, 2026.</p><p>Waiting until the last minute can lead to mistakes, delays in your refund, and a higher audit risk if it's done in a rush. The sooner you file, the sooner you get your refund.</p><h2>Documents You'll Need</h2><ul><li>Form W-2 (from your employer)</li><li>Form 1099 (if you are an independent contractor)</li><li>Social Security Number (SSN) or ITIN</li><li>Dependent information (children, family members)</li><li>Prior-year tax return (if applicable)</li></ul><h2>Important Credits and Benefits for Latino Families</h2><p>Many taxpayers lose money every year by not knowing about these benefits:</p><h3>Child Tax Credit (CTC)</h3><p>Can significantly reduce what you owe or increase your refund.</p><h3>Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC)</h3><p>Especially important for independent workers and moderate-income families.</p><h3>Self-Employment Deductions</h3><p>If you work as a contractor, drive for Uber or DoorDash, or work in construction, cleaning, or run a small business, you can deduct expenses and legally pay less in taxes.</p><h2>Did You Buy a Home This Year?</h2><p>If you bought a home, you may benefit from the mortgage interest deduction, property taxes, and points paid at closing. Many generic preparers don't explain these benefits correctly.</p><h2>Common Mistakes We See Every Season</h2><ol><li>Filing without checking available credits</li><li>Not reporting 1099 income correctly</li><li>Using inexperienced preparers</li><li>Not planning ahead if you own a business</li></ol><p>A mistake can trigger IRS letters months later.</p><h2>Why Work With a Professional?</h2><p>In the Latino community, it's common to hear: "My cousin does my taxes" or "I use cheap software." But when problems come up, no one is there to answer for it.</p><p>At Guzman Tax & Accounting, we offer personalized service in Spanish, a clear explanation of the process, accurate and responsible preparation, assistance if you receive an IRS letter, and strategies to legally pay less. We don't just fill out forms — we protect your financial stability.</p><h2>Schedule Your Appointment Today</h2><p>Peak season fills up fast. The sooner you file, the sooner you get your money. Call us today or book your appointment online — don't wait until the last minute.</p><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Schedule Your Consultation</a></div>
